    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = x+yx^{2}, \left(1,1\right), \left(-3,4\right), \left(-4,4\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(1,1\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-3,4\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-4,4\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>33</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>60</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(1,1\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(1,1) = 1  + 1(1)^{2} = 2</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(-3,4\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-3,4) = -3  + 4(-3)^{2} = 33</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(-4,4\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-4,4) = -4  + 4(-4)^{2} = 60</m>.


</solution>
